==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar|en}} {{term|حسین|tr=ḥusayn|lang=ar}}, from the root {{ar-root|ح|س|ن}}.

===Alternative forms===
* [[Husain]]
* [[Husein]]
* [[Hussain]]
* [[Hussein]]

===Proper noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{Islam}} A son of [[Ali]] and brother of [[Hassan]]; a [[martyr]], and [[Shiah]] [[Imam]].
# {{given name|male|from=Arabic}} used by [[Muslim]]s, diminutive of Hasan {{Arab|[[حسن]]}} meaning ''[[good]]'' or ''[[handsome]]''.
# {{surname|[[Muslim]]|from=Arabic|dot=}} derived from the {{etyl|ar|en}} given name.

====Usage notes====
* Used by both [[Sunni]] and [[Shiah]] Muslims

====Usage notes====
* In Hebrew, Chasin is a [[given name]] meaning ''strong'' and also appears in liturgy meaning 'mighty.'
* In Hebrew, the word ''chassan'' means ''groom'', as in 'bride and groom' , and though the two [chasin - chasan] have a different spelling, they share the same pronunciation.

